aarch64: do not pack struct epoll_event, or every kqueue event misroutes.

This is the true root of #15 (the teardown hang AND the ciderd-teardown CPU spin that 0004-0007 in
libkqueue were only bounding). The guest's linux epoll_event was `__attribute__((packed))`
unconditionally -- the x86_64 layout (12 bytes, 8-byte data at offset 4). The Linux kernel packs
epoll_event ONLY on x86_64 (uapi/linux/eventpoll.h: EPOLL_PACKED is packed under __x86_64__, empty
otherwise); on aarch64 __u64 data aligns to 8, so the struct is 16 bytes with data at offset 8.

With the packed guest struct on an aarch64 host, the kernel read (and wrote) the 8-byte data field at
offset 8 while the guest stored it at offset 4. Every knote pointer libkqueue passes as epoll_event.data
therefore came back mangled, and because all guest knote pointers share their high 32 bits
(0x40000266f2d0, 0x40000266f3c0, ...), they all collapsed to the SAME value (0xdf7c00004000 observed) --
so distinct knotes aliased one epoll registration. That misrouting is exactly the observed failures:
EVFILT_PROC/NOTE_EXIT for the shell was delivered as the wrong filter, so shellspawn never saw the exit
and the launcher hung; and a freed knote's descriptor kept firing under a live knote's pointer, the
100% CPU epoll spin.

Fix: gate the packing on __x86_64__, matching the kernel per arch. Confirmed by CIDER_TRACE_KNOTE
(patch 0007): knote_new returns distinct pointers, but the host epoll_ctl recorded one shared data value.
---
--- a/darling/src/libsystem_kernel/emulation/include/linux_premigration/ext/sys/epoll.h
+++ b/darling/src/libsystem_kernel/emulation/include/linux_premigration/ext/sys/epoll.h
@@ -43,11 +43,21 @@
 	uint64_t u64;
 } epoll_data_t;
 
+/* The kernel packs epoll_event ONLY on x86_64 (uapi eventpoll.h): 12 bytes, data at offset 4.
+ * Everywhere else (aarch64) it is unpacked: __u64 data aligns to 8, so 16 bytes, data at offset 8.
+ * Packing unconditionally made the aarch64 kernel read/write data at the wrong offset, collapsing
+ * every distinct data pointer to the same value and misrouting every kqueue event (#15). */
+#if defined(__x86_64__)
+#	define CIDER_EPOLL_PACKED __attribute__((packed))
+#else
+#	define CIDER_EPOLL_PACKED
+#endif
+
 struct epoll_event
 {
 	uint32_t events;
 	epoll_data_t data;
-} __attribute__((packed));
+} CIDER_EPOLL_PACKED;
 
 extern int epoll_create (int __size) __THROW;
 
